ector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nFind $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-2,\\,y(t)={t}^{2}+t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 6+7\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =-2+12+84 \\\\  & =94.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c51be72e720acdf684d781a60c473ee08cf3474393efa14c9322ca218581551"} {"question" "q-42249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-61"] ["math" "-92"] ["math" "76"] ["math" "84"] ["math" "94"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "94"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$ Find $⟨{sin}^{2}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨{sin}^{2}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}]-[\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c51be72e720acdf684d781a60c473ee08cf3474393efa14c9322ca218581551"} {"question" "q-42254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-139997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[0,\\pi ],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,\\pi ].$ Find $⟨t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-139997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for the integration by parts, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t){|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡0)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =0+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-139997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c51be72e720acdf684d781a60c473ee08cf3474393efa14c9322ca218581551"} {"question" "q-139997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-139997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-139997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[0,2],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,2].$ Find $⟨t,{e}^{t}⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨t,{e}^{t}⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2}t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{t} & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for the integration by parts, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{0}^{2}-{\\int }_{0}^{2}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t{e}^{t}){|}_{0}^{2}-{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2{e}^{2}-0{e}^{0})-{e}^{t}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}-({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c51be72e720acdf684d781a60c473ee08cf3474393efa14c9322ca218581551"} {"question" "q-42256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{2}"] ["math" "{e}^{2}+1"] ["math" "{e}^{2}-2"] ["math" "{e}^{t}+1"] ["math" "{e}^{t}-t+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{2}+1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].$ Find $⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,{cos}^{2}⁡t⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,{cos}^{2}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{(1)^{3}}{3}]-[-\\frac{(0)^{3}}{3}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c51be72e720acdf684d781a60c473ee08cf3474393efa14c9322ca218581551"} {"question" "q-42255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-42255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-43855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[-1,0],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-1,0].$ Find $⟨t,\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-43855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨t,\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{0}t\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=1-{t}^{2},$ $\\text{d}u=-2t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}t\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & =-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3/2}]-[-\\frac{1}{3}(0)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-43855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c51be72e720acdf684d781a60c473ee08cf3474393efa14c9322ca218581551"} {"question" "q-43855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-43855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "q-43855" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5322815966e3cf981348426cbca53f2ecb0b9f30bcaadfa2a478866cccd2ff0"} {"question" "e-5542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An inner product on $V = \\mathbb{R}^3$ is given by $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle =  3 x_1 y_1 + x_2 y_2 + 7 x_3 y_3.$ Find $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle,$ if\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/assets/028bb3befd54071fcae6cb88bd3e054d3325557ef31274ec23146e1da81f8258.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/example-5542.json" "file_sha256" "db05b55b6e06891e4da5abda2082e8d7295d70d7bd536246bcf62cccc92b57fe"} {"question" "e-5542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+7{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-3)+(-2)\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 0\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-9-2+0 \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/example-5542.json" "file_sha256" "db05b55b6e06891e4da5abda2082e8d7295d70d7bd536246bcf62cccc92b57fe"} {"question" "e-5543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=\\mathbb{R}_2[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n\\langle {x}(t), {y}(t) \\rangle = x(1)y(1) + x(2)y(2) + x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\n Find $\\langle \\mathbf{x}(t), \\mathbf{y}(t) \\rangle,$ if\n\n$$\n{x}(t) = 1-2t+3t^2,\n\t\\quad\n\t{y}(t) = t-t^2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/example-5543.json" "file_sha256" "dbc6c5789a704fdd19cb3d2c07eafc8ba541a816059ac44de25852e193ecd617"} {"question" "e-5543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+9\\cdot (-2)+22\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =0-18-132 \\\\  & =-150.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/example-5543.json" "file_sha256" "dbc6c5789a704fdd19cb3d2c07eafc8ba541a816059ac44de25852e193ecd617"} {"question" "e-5544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=\\mathcal{C}\\left[0,2\\pi\\right],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $\\left[0,2\\pi\\right].$ Find $\\langle \\sin t, \\cos t \\rangle$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\langle x(t),y(t) \\rangle = \\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{2\\pi} x(t) y(t) \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/example-5544.json" "file_sha256" "66e3e4b9f17938aaf8591eb842a371f8b3a52e7f745bebbb79955c8485f6be28"} {"question" "e-5544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n\\langle \\sin t, \\cos t \\rangle  =  \\int_{0}^{2\\pi}\\sin{t} \\cos{t} \\,\\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the identity $\\sin2t =2\\sin t\\cos t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(1-1) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/example-5544.json" "file_sha256" "66e3e4b9f17938aaf8591eb842a371f8b3a52e7f745bebbb79955c8485f6be28"}] "usage" {"e-5542" [] "e-5544" [] "q-42250" [] "q-42249" [] "q-42248" [] "q-42256" [] "e-5543" [] "q-42254" []} "basis" 1835 "retractions" [[17592186134306 :question/problem "An inner product on $V = R^{3}$ is given by $⟨x, y⟩ = 2x_{1}y_{1} + x_{2}y_{2} + 9x_{3}y_{3}$. Find $⟨x, y⟩$, if\n\n$x = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, y = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186134307 :question/problem "Let $V = R_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product\n\n$⟨x(t), y(t)⟩ = x(-1)y(-1) + x(0)y(0) + x(1)y(1)$.\nFind $⟨x(t), y(t)⟩$, if\n$x(t) = 5 - 2t + t^{2}, y(t) = t - 1$."] [17592186134309 :question/problem "Let $V = C[- \\frac{π}{2}, \\frac{π}{2}]$, the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[- \\frac{π}{2}, \\frac{π}{2}]$. Find $⟨\\sin^{2} t, \\cos t⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$⟨x(t), y(t)⟩ = ∫_{- π/2}^{π/2}x(t)y(t)dt$."] [17592186134310 :question/problem "Let $V = C[0, 2]$, the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0, 2]$. Find $⟨t, e^{t}⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$⟨x(t), y(t)⟩ = ∫_{0}^{2}x(t)y(t)dt$."] [17592186133492 :question/problem "An inner product on $V = \\mathbb{R}^3$ is given by $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle = 3 x_1 y_1 + x_2 y_2 + 7 x_3 y_3$. Find $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle$, if\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186133492 :question/worked-solution "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n⟨x, y⟩ &= 3x_{1}y_{1} + x_{2}y_{2} + 7x_{3}y_{3} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-3) + (-2) \\cdot 1 + 7 \\cdot 0 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=-9 - 2 + 0 \\\\\n&=-11\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133493 :question/problem "Let $V=\\mathbb{R}_2[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product\n$\\langle {x}(t), {y}(t) \\rangle = x(1)y(1) + x(2)y(2) + x(3)y(3)$.\nFind $\\langle \\mathbf{x}(t), \\mathbf{y}(t) \\rangle$, if\n${x}(t) = 1-2t+3t^2, \\quad {y}(t) = t-t^2$."] [17592186133493 :question/worked-solution "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n⟨x(t), y(t)⟩ &= x(1)y(1) + x(2)y(2) + x(3)y(3) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 0 + 9 \\cdot (-2) + 22 \\cdot (-6) \\\\\n&= 0 - 18 - 132 \\\\\n&=-150\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133494 :question/problem "Let $V=\\mathcal{C}\\left[0,2\\pi\\right]$, the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $\\left[0,2\\pi\\right]$. Find $\\langle \\sin t, \\cos t \\rangle$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n$\\langle x(t),y(t) \\rangle = \\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{2\\pi} x(t) y(t) \\, \\textrm{d}t$."] [17592186133494 :question/worked-solution "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n\\langle \\sin t, \\cos t \\rangle = \\int_{0}^{2\\pi}\\sin{t} \\cos{t} \\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the identity\n\n$$\n\\sin2t =2\\sin t\\cos t\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2π}\\sin t\\cos tdt &= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{0}^{2π}\\sin 2tdt \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}\\cos 2t \\mid _{0}^{2π} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(\\cos 4π - \\cos 0) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(1 - 1) \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186132279 17592186132280 17592186132281 17592186132282 17592186132283 17592186132285 17592186132286 17592186132287 17592186132288 17592186132289 17592186132297 17592186132298 17592186132299 17592186132300 17592186132301 17592186132303 17592186132304 17592186132305 17592186132306 17592186132307 17592186294757 17592186294758 17592186294759 17592186294760 17592186294761] "immutable_fields" [[17592186132278 :answer-field/correct] [17592186132278 :answer-field/id] [17592186132278 :answer-field/key] [17592186132278 :answer-field/type] [17592186132284 :answer-field/correct] [17592186132284 :answer-field/id] [17592186132284 :answer-field/key] [17592186132284 :answer-field/type] [17592186132296 :answer-field/correct] [17592186132296 :answer-field/id] [17592186132296 :answer-field/key] [17592186132296 :answer-field/type] [17592186132302 :answer-field/correct] [17592186132302 :answer-field/id] [17592186132302 :answer-field/key] [17592186132302 :answer-field/type] [17592186294756 :answer-field/correct] [17592186294756 :answer-field/id] [17592186294756 :answer-field/key] [17592186294756 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
